        "id": 1256783
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-27T05:41:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oops sorry, brackets removed.\n\nThere isn\u0027t a vendor command to read the data, as it can be done by reading the NVRAM space (eg with tpmc) - so I don\u0027t plan to add support for reading here. \n\nI\u0027m guessing the convention for the args is due to the way getopt_long parses the command line.",
      "parentUuid": "c2717428_b38117b5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "deb87c98cdf45d32b657a9b2dfbeb42190bbed1f",
