    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ab486de_180fd5e4",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/gsctool.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1161144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-28T00:43:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re going to need to have access to the SN Bits and RMA count on the factory and RMA floors, and also as part of Chrome OS startup (e.g. https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r1lO653UNIDqoj_oVtED5wLQFp5b_4igdVtaA1G25jU/edit#heading\u003dh.f2h7486rvn5s where the idea would be to use, e.g. gsctool -S to see if we have SN Bits that are not simply all f).\n\nIIRC, using tpmc is a bit arcane, but more importantly requires knowing the exact addresses to look at (and maybe some address translation too)? I don\u0027t think that\u0027s something that is friendly for the above use cases. Could this be done inside gsctool instead even without a vendor command? Or would we need a vendor command?",
      "parentUuid": "7d9fde1e_94ed26cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "deb87c98cdf45d32b657a9b2dfbeb42190bbed1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e9c00da_2dc477d5",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/gsctool.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1256783
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-28T01:04:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yea I can see it\u0027s a little weird to have writes but not reads here, but AFAICT this tool currently only sends vendor commands or performs device maintenance, I guess it\u0027s nicer to avoid adding unnecessary clutter to it. \n\nIf ease of use is the concern, maybe we can add a simple script that wraps the relevant tpmc call? It should be just a line or two.\n\nThe addresses won\u0027t change, so baking them into a script should not be a problem.\n\ntpmc read \u003cindex\u003e \u003csize\u003e\n\nboard id:\ntpmc read 0x3fff00 0xc\n\nsn bits:\ntpmc read 0x3fff01 0x10\n\nIf you want a single entry point for managing sn bits, perhaps that script can also wrap the gsctool commands for writes",
      "parentUuid": "4ab486de_180fd5e4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "deb87c98cdf45d32b657a9b2dfbeb42190bbed1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad1cde33_2dad55c0",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/gsctool.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-28T01:18:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the only issue with tpmc that it requires trunksd stopped, so the factory scripts need to take care of that and then restarting the daemon. gsctool works with and without trunksd running.\nwe can teach tpmc to send commands to trunksd if it\u0027s running, but that\u0027s a separate thing.",
      "parentUuid": "3e9c00da_2dc477d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "deb87c98cdf45d32b657a9b2dfbeb42190bbed1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
