    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60248538_a0aa07bd",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/gsctool.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1161144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-28T02:11:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To apronin\u0027s comment (in case reading doesn\u0027t make it into gsctool but instead into some other command/script per louiscollard\u0027s suggestion): What happens while trunksd is stopped? We need to check SN Bits during Chrome OS startup too (to provide a new key/value pair to the session manager). Would stopping trunksd then if it is running (and later restarting it) risk breaking things now or later?",
      "parentUuid": "255bd7eb_57f0680e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "deb87c98cdf45d32b657a9b2dfbeb42190bbed1f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5d8d18f_55dcc9ec",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/gsctool.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 547,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-28T02:19:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, we shouldn\u0027t be stopping/restarting trunksd outside of debug/testing (and possibly factory) environment. so, unless it is done before trunksd is started, tpmc won\u0027t work for those scenarios.\n\ndidn\u0027t realize we need to pass it to session_manager for some reason. and, generally, yes, calling some CLI tool in upstart script is better than making session_manager call tpm_manager over dbus to read nvram, assuming that\u0027s ok from the critical path performance point of view. if we add reading SN to session_manager\u0027s pre-start, (a) this time will be added to time before login-visible, (b) session_manager\u0027s upstart will need to be made tpm-version-aware as gsctool is available only for cr50 (not just USE\u003dtpm2, but USE\u003dcr50_onboard).",
      "parentUuid": "60248538_a0aa07bd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 547,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 547,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "deb87c98cdf45d32b657a9b2dfbeb42190bbed1f",
